seg-10fac3e641e0 = writes <c1/> and <c2/> (<c3/> changes the name). The inputs are result files from earlier runs: a scenario run writes <c4/> beside <c5/>, and <c6/> writes its own. The kind of each run is read from the scenario file beside the result, from the content of a receiver-trust result, or from a top-level <c7/>, and must be a kind the engine knows. A result is listed as not used, with the reason, and counts for nothing when its kind cannot be found, is not a known kind, or the sibling scenario and the result's own <c8/> disagree. (The result's <c9/> and a hash of the scenario file are not compared: the engine computes the first over its parsed scenario and a file hash is over the text, so they are different quantities.)

